Z||000000||SibERThuG||06-18-2000||11:13 PM||||I'm looking for ground effects. Anyone know where I can get them. (no, <A HREF="http://www.groundeffects.com" TARGET=_blank>www.groundeffects.com</A>  doesn't have them.) I'm also looking for a sub/box that will fit in my car. I'm 6'4" and one will not fit behind my seat. Any suggestions on how to fit a sub(s) in?? Anyone with any of these for sale e-mail me at slimm_shadee@hotmail.com||||reg||12
Z||000001||stimpy||06-19-2000||12:02 AM||||As far as the sub goes, I just recently completed a project where I built a fiberglass enclosure that fits down in the passenger footwell. It holds a Polk Audio dX10, a 10" sub designed for small enclosures. If you look in the general fiero chat for my thread "has anybody made a footwell sub enclosure" I gave a journal-type rundown of the process. Actually it was easy money, and I had never worked with fiberglass before.  <BR>I think that this is the best compromise when putting in a subwoofer.  People have built special enclosures behind the seat by cutting out a bit of the "false" firewall, others have made bandpass boxes for the front compartment. Both of these methods do involve some cutting, and I'm not in to hacking up my car. (Don't have that kind of confidence)<BR>I am also tall (6'6"), but can still sit in the passenger seat comfortably with my sub in place. And it does POUND! Good luck in your projects and welcome to the forum.||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||06-19-2000||09:48 AM||||my sub box is located about like stimpy's but i'm using a jl audio 8. i'm considering adding more,but it sounds pretty good as is. <P>i'm trying to piece together some ground effects. i've got the irm integrated rocker panel for the side. i'll probaly get a regular gt rear facia (got a line on one i think if i can get my money to cooperate), because there's almost nothing else available. pisa makes a couple of front end variations, but they're kind of tame. i'm still looking myself.<P>if you've got $3000 you might consider an imsa type kit. focoa has them and i think irm.<p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-19-2000).]||||reg||1
